+# Research
+
+## Request path and current behavior
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/category/CategoryApi.java` maps `DELETE /api/v1/private/category/{id}` to `CategoryFacade.deleteCategory(id, merchantStore)` and maps `GET /api/v1/category/{id}` to the facade. The facade throws `ResourceNotFoundException` for missing categories on reads, while delete currently resolves the category through a different helper that does not validate the store id.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/category/CategoryFacadeImpl.java` delegates deletion to `CategoryService.delete`. Category product listing already checks for a missing category and throws 404, but stale/deleted category handling depends on deletion completing cleanly.
+- Category hierarchy listing uses category rows and lineage, so deleting the root and descendants removes them from `GET /api/v1/category` when the category subtree is actually deleted.
+
+## Root cause
+
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/category/CategoryServiceImpl.java` builds the category subtree from the root lineage, loads products associated with any subtree category, and then:
+  - removes category links only when a product has more than one category;
+  - deletes the product when it has one/no remaining category.
+- This directly violates product retention and explains missing products, broken cart/order references, and product detail failures.
+- The product-to-category mapping is `Product.categories` in `sm-core-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/model/catalog/product/Product.java`, backed by `PRODUCT_CATEGORY`. It has refresh/detach-style cascade settings, not delete cascade, so links must be removed before deleting categories. Product rows, inventory, prices, variants, and order/cart rows must not be deleted.
+- `Category.categories` has `CascadeType.REMOVE`, so deleting the root category is intended to delete descendants. The service must remove product links for every category in the subtree and then delete the category tree.
+
+## Related behavior and affected areas
+
+- Product category searches in `ProductServiceImpl`/`ProductRepositoryImpl` join `p.categories`; removing links makes deleted-category product listings empty while retaining products for other categories.
+- Product v2 population reads product categories, so the removed links naturally disappear from `GET /api/v2/product/{sku}`.
+- Shopping cart and order services reference products and use product data for calculations; deleting only category links preserves those references and their stock/price data.
+- Existing category integration coverage in `sm-shop/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/shop/integration/category/CategoryManagementAPIIntegrationTest.java` is minimal and does not cover product retention, subtree deletion, missing-category 404, or cart/order continuity.
+
+## Planned files
+
+- Change the category deletion service (and, if needed, its facade lookup) so deletion is store-scoped, missing ids remain 404, all subtree product links are detached, no product is deleted, and the subtree categories are deleted.
+- Add focused regression coverage at the service/integration level for product retention and category 404/listing behavior, reusing existing test infrastructure where practical.
